  "inbox_context": "Company crypto news/media operation with several separate brands, each with its own business mailbox (Altcoin Informer, Coinography, Memecoinist). Each mailbox has its own purpose, reply knowledge and sender identity: judge and answer a message ONLY with that mailbox's own context, and never reuse one brand's pricing, links, signature, services or policies for another.",
  "account_purposes": {
    "sales": "sales@coinography.com \u2014 Coinography sales inbox. Goal: close paid ads/sponsorships on coinography.com (banners, sponsored content, newsletter sponsorship, social campaigns). IMPORTANT when someone asks pricing, rates, media kit, how much to advertise/post, or wants a package. NOISE: product manufacturers, procurement RFQs, SEO link sellers.",
    "coinography": "info@coinography.com \u2014 Coinography general/info inbox for the crypto news site. Same revenue model: paid advertising & sponsored posts. IMPORTANT: ad inquiries, rate questions, press-release buys, replies from advertisers. Also site/account/security issues. NOISE: cold RFQ spam, fake partnership blasts, newsletters.",
    "memecoinist": "sales@memecoinist.com \u2014 Memecoinist sales for memecoin news/promo site. Revenue from paid listings, sponsored memecoin articles, promo posts, and ads. IMPORTANT: listing requests, how much to get featured/posted, PR packages for meme coins/tokens. NOISE: unrelated RFQs, SEO spam, generic partnership templates.",
    "altcoininformer": "info@altcoininformer.com - Altcoin Informer, a cryptocurrency-focused news and media mailbox. Purpose: receive and manage the business correspondence of the Altcoin Informer media business. CRITICAL: genuine account-security incidents, compromised access or urgent operational disruptions, serious payment or service failures. IMPORTANT: legitimate advertising and sponsorship enquiries, paying customer requests, time-sensitive partnership opportunities, customer support needing a response, relevant business enquiries. NORMAL: general correspondence, non-urgent operational messages, routine business updates. NOISE: irrelevant promotional outreach, unsolicited bulk marketing, obvious spam and unrelated offers. Initial guidance, not rigid rules: weigh sender identity, message context and evidence."
  },
